hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"303","Narrated by Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala Al-Attar, narrated by Sufyan, who said: I heard Al-Zuhri, saying: Urwa bin Al-Zubayr told me that he heard Aisha She says: “Prayer was first assumed to be two rak’ahs, then the travel prayer was established, and the urban prayer was completed.” So I said to Urwa: What was the matter with her? Done? He said: It interpreted what Othman interpreted. Sa`id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzoumi told us about it. Sufyan told us, in a different way, that he said in all of them: On the authority of"
"304","Yunus bin Muadh Al-Aqdi told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Bukayr bin Al-Akhnas, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “God made it obligatory Prayer on the tongue of your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, four rak’ahs in the city, two rak’ahs when traveling, and one rak’ah in fear.”"
